  "title": "Lesson 2: Contact vs Non-Contact Forces",
  "explanation": "Forces are either contact forces (push, pull, friction, normal, tension, buoyancy) or non-contact forces (gravity, magnetism, electrostatic). Contact means surfaces or connected materials must interact. Non-contact means invisible fields bridge the gap — gravity pulls downward, magnets tug across air, and charged objects attract without touching.",
